  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + ViT-L + multiprofile as the best model family (0.715–0.721 acc), with concat fusion and transformer aggregation as the top settings (config_038 at 0.721). Config_039 (transformer aggregation + weighted fusion) is the only remaining untested configuration in this top family, completing the 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid. While prior evidence suggests concat > weighted (0.721 vs 0.706 for transformer; 0.715 vs 0.706 for avgpool), testing this final cell confirms whether the interaction between transformer aggregation and weighted fusion could yield an unexpected synergy. As the last experiment in the budget, this is the most targeted exploitation of the strongest evidence, ensuring no untested variant in the best-performing family is left unexplored. All other untested configurations involve inferior encoders (scgpt, PCA) or a much weaker image encoder (ResNet50, which scored only 0.208 image-only), making them very unlikely to surpass 0.721."
